menu "Muse multi-app demo"

    config MUSE_APPS_DEMO
        bool "M5Stack multi-app demo UI (launcher + Pet World + diagnostics + hardware demo)"
        # Its apps draw captions in a 5x7 ASCII font, a few short lines at a
        # time: not CJK or accented letters, nor full-screen reply pages.
        depends on MUSE_BOARD_M5STACK_CORE2 && SPIRAM && !MUSE_SMALL_FULL_REPLY
        depends on !MUSE_CJK_FONT && !MUSE_LATIN_FONT
        default n
        help
            Draw a touch-driven launcher and three sample apps as the face,
            inside the normal muse_ui flow (so sleep, brightness and the pairing
            prompt keep working): Pet World (an animated pet with day/night
            rooms and speech bubbles tied to the voice session), a diagnostics
            app (real Wi-Fi and Noise/session status, a signal-level meter, a
            speaker beep and a connection test), and a hardware app (battery and
            chip info, a touch physics canvas, an audio-level meter). A 320x240
            RGB565 framebuffer in PSRAM is drawn full-screen each frame.
            Intended as an example of building a custom UI on the board's
            display; leave disabled for the standard avatar interface.

endmenu
